# Docker ignore rules for AgentOS backend images.
#
# IMPORTANT: the images are built with the REPOSITORY ROOT as the build context
# (they need the root `acbe/` package), so Docker does not read this file for them.
# BuildKit (the default builder in Docker 23+ and Compose v2) instead uses the
# Dockerfile-specific ignore files that sit next to each Dockerfile:
#
#   backend/Dockerfile.dockerignore                      (API / worker / scheduler)
#   backend/deploy/docker/Dockerfile.browser.dockerignore (browser worker)
#
# Those replace the root .dockerignore for these builds. This file applies when
# `backend/` itself is used as a build context (e.g. tooling or dev containers);
# every pattern uses `**/` so it is valid for either context. Keep the three files
# in sync. The Dockerfiles only COPY explicit paths, so these rules mainly keep
# secrets and bulky local state out of the build context that is sent to the builder.

# Secrets and local environment
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/secrets/

# VCS / editors
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.github
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# Python build and cache artefacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/*.egg-info
**/build
**/dist
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov

# Local runtime state (local object storage, databases, load-test output)
**/.data
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/traces
**/loadtest-results

# Not needed inside images
**/node_modules
**/tests
**/docs
**/deploy/k8s
**/deploy/terraform
